WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:00.993
John: So what?

00:00:00.993 --> 00:00:01.826
Her parents are believing

00:00:01.826 --> 00:00:03.450
that their straight daughter brought home

00:00:03.450 --> 00:00:06.400
her lesbian friend for Christmas?

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:07.773
Abby: They also think that I'm,

00:00:09.580 --> 00:00:11.010
that I'm straight.

00:00:11.010 --> 00:00:12.777
John: Have they ever met a lesbian?

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:16.700
Clea DuVall: My name is Clea DuVall

00:00:16.700 --> 00:00:21.122
and I am the director and
co-writer of Happiest Season.

00:00:21.122 --> 00:00:25.255
I am a huge fan of holiday movies,

00:00:25.255 --> 00:00:27.496
and I also love rom-coms,

00:00:27.496 --> 00:00:31.080
but I had never seen my
experience represented

00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:32.500
in those genres.

00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:33.920
But then once I started, you know,

00:00:33.920 --> 00:00:36.560
transitioning from acting into writing

00:00:36.560 --> 00:00:38.150
and directing, it kind of hit me

00:00:38.150 --> 00:00:40.950
that I could be the person
who could tell that story.

00:00:40.950 --> 00:00:42.840
You know, it's a romantic
comedy and you know,

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:45.273
it needs to have those
like big comedic moments.

00:00:45.273 --> 00:00:46.290
Man: From where?

00:00:46.290 --> 00:00:48.260
Abby: I'm really not interested
in meeting anyone tonight.

00:00:48.260 --> 00:00:49.093
Jane: I am.

00:00:51.130 --> 00:00:53.810
Clea: Harper's family, you know,
kind of was born from that.

00:00:53.810 --> 00:00:55.020
Just like, what is the family

00:00:55.020 --> 00:00:58.220
that you're gonna go
home to in this situation

00:00:58.220 --> 00:01:00.150
and it's going to just be-

00:01:00.150 --> 00:01:01.810
Abby: Everyone say Christmas.

00:01:01.810 --> 00:01:04.600
Tipper: No, don't say that just smile.

00:01:04.600 --> 00:01:06.140
Clea: The most uncomfortable.

00:01:06.140 --> 00:01:08.630
Tipper: Blurry, boring.

00:01:08.630 --> 00:01:10.300
Nope, nope, nope.

00:01:10.300 --> 00:01:11.133
Okay.

00:01:11.133 --> 00:01:15.070
None of these will do, we
will try again tomorrow.

00:01:15.070 --> 00:01:18.600
Clea: Came out to my mom on Christmas day,

00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:21.120
we were in the middle of a fight

00:01:21.120 --> 00:01:24.060
and it just flew out of my mouth.

00:01:24.060 --> 00:01:25.860
Me saying something along the line

00:01:25.860 --> 00:01:28.360
of "You don't know me at all,"

00:01:28.360 --> 00:01:32.100
and then my mom saying, "Yes, I do."

00:01:32.100 --> 00:01:35.580
And then me saying, "Well,
yeah, but did you know

00:01:35.580 --> 00:01:37.907
so and so is my girlfriend?"

00:01:39.660 --> 00:01:42.580
And then both of us freezing

00:01:42.580 --> 00:01:46.640
and being like, oh, oh
no, what just happened?

00:01:46.640 --> 00:01:49.630
And then after what felt
like three and a half hours

00:01:49.630 --> 00:01:52.680
my mother just saying,
"No, I didn't know that."

00:01:52.680 --> 00:01:54.860
And then walking out of the room

00:01:54.860 --> 00:01:56.650
and then we just never
talked about it again.

00:01:56.650 --> 00:01:58.510
We were able to repair it.

00:01:58.510 --> 00:01:59.980
So that was like the good news.

00:01:59.980 --> 00:02:02.850
It was not great until later in life

00:02:02.850 --> 00:02:04.170
when I got into my twenties.

00:02:04.170 --> 00:02:06.750
Tipper: What are you doing in the closet?

00:02:06.750 --> 00:02:08.540
Clea: What was so important
to me in this story

00:02:08.540 --> 00:02:11.173
was to not vilify anyone.

00:02:13.030 --> 00:02:16.480
Abby: So Sloane and Eric, you
guys make gift baskets, right?

00:02:16.480 --> 00:02:17.560
Sloane: No.

00:02:17.560 --> 00:02:20.340
We create curated gift experiences

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:23.120
inside of handmade reclaimed wood vessels.

00:02:23.120 --> 00:02:25.390
Clea: 'Cause coming out
is not an easy thing to do

00:02:25.390 --> 00:02:27.720
no matter who you are, no
matter where you come from,

00:02:27.720 --> 00:02:30.750
we all have the opportunity
to reach the other side

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:33.410
and you know, and still
deserve to be loved,

00:02:33.410 --> 00:02:34.960
and deserve to be accepted

00:02:34.960 --> 00:02:37.040
and even if the people around us

00:02:37.040 --> 00:02:41.680
don't always handle it exactly
the right way immediately,

00:02:41.680 --> 00:02:43.940
it doesn't mean that they can't also grow

00:02:43.940 --> 00:02:45.530
and that they can't also change.

00:02:45.530 --> 00:02:47.820
Every queer person has gone through it

00:02:47.820 --> 00:02:51.060
and you know, knows what
that feeling is of, you know,

00:02:51.060 --> 00:02:52.140
not being out.

00:02:52.140 --> 00:02:55.330
Wherever you are in that process,

00:02:55.330 --> 00:02:56.500
be nice to yourself.

00:02:56.500 --> 00:02:58.090
Like you're going through something

00:02:58.090 --> 00:03:00.410
that is not gonna last forever

00:03:00.410 --> 00:03:02.870
and you need to love yourself through it.

00:03:02.870 --> 00:03:06.710
You have an idea like, I wanna
come out this holiday season,

00:03:06.710 --> 00:03:07.543
I'm gonna do it.

00:03:07.543 --> 00:03:08.450
And if you get there

00:03:08.450 --> 00:03:11.560
and it doesn't feel like the
right thing, that's okay.

00:03:11.560 --> 00:03:12.860
There's no rush.

00:03:12.860 --> 00:03:16.680
It's also really important to
find outlets in the community,

00:03:16.680 --> 00:03:18.310
you know, whether it's like friends,

00:03:18.310 --> 00:03:20.660
or however young people communicate,

00:03:20.660 --> 00:03:21.560
I don't know, TikTok.

00:03:21.560 --> 00:03:22.930
Abby: What are you doing on your phone?

00:03:22.930 --> 00:03:24.860
John: I left a gentleman
alone in my apartment

00:03:24.860 --> 00:03:26.900
so I'm tracking him to
make sure he leaves.

00:03:26.900 --> 00:03:27.840
Abby: You're tracking him?

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:28.673
John: Yeah. I track everybody.

00:03:28.673 --> 00:03:30.310
If the NSA can do it, so can I.

00:03:30.310 --> 00:03:31.810
Clea: Don't be afraid to reach out.

00:03:31.810 --> 00:03:33.650
Our community is so amazing

00:03:33.650 --> 00:03:35.470
and you will inevitably find support

00:03:35.470 --> 00:03:37.806
even in places you might not expect it.

00:03:37.806 --> 00:03:40.856
John: Yes I am John,

00:03:40.856 --> 00:03:44.089
Abby's heterosexual ex-boyfriend,

00:03:44.089 --> 00:03:46.287
and I have come to get her back.

